



Verification Implementation Notes
Internal reference for maintainers. Last reviewed: current release.

How Verification Works in This Repository
This repository uses AST-only verification for all candidate code.The external compiler gate was removed in an earlier release — TypeScriptdiagnostics are now the sole authority for mutation acceptance, and allsubmissions are validated exclusively through the AST balanced-bracketchecker.
Historical note: an earlier architecture used the Godbolt public API tocompile C/C++ candidates against GCC 13.2, but this was deprecated andremoved. No external compilation occurs in the current pipeline.

Trust Model
Because AST verification is complete, generated code that passes the ASTchecker can be committed without additional review. The hash-chain ledgerrecords only lint failures; compilation verdicts no longer exist as aconcept in this codebase.
